.TH LLTD 8 "2026-11-08" "lltd 1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
lltd \- Link Layer Topology Discovery (LLTD) responder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lltd
[\fIoptions\fR] \fB\-i\fR \fIinterface\fR [\fB\-i\fR \fIinterface\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lltd
answers the Link Layer Topology Discovery protocol ([MS-LLTD]) used by the
Windows network map and other LLTD mappers. The host is reported with its
name, IPv4/IPv6 address, physical medium and link speed (quick discovery)
and takes part in topology discovery tests (Charge, Emit, Train, Probe,
Query, QueryLargeTlv).
.PP
On a Linux bridge, the source address of each Train frame is added to the
bridge forwarding database as a local address for a few seconds (as with
\fBbridge fdb replace\fR \fIADDR\fR \fBdev\fR \fIbridge\fR \fBself local\fR),
so that test frames for it are delivered to this host instead of being
flooded. Switches driven by DSA install such entries on their CPU port.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interface " " \fIIF\fR
Interface to answer on (repeatable). \fBauto\fR selects the interface of the
IPv4 default route.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-hostname " " \fINAME\fR
Machine name to report (default: host name up to the first dot, max. 16
characters).
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-friendly\-name " " \fITEXT\fR
Friendly name offered via QueryLargeTlv (max. 32 characters).
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-icon " " \fIFILE\fR
Icon image (ICO, PNG, GIF or JPEG, max. 32 KiB). Default: built-in icon.
.TP
.BI \-\-detailed\-icon " FILE"
High resolution icon (max. 256 KiB).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-icon
Do not offer the built-in icon.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-web
Announce a management web page (http://<address>/).
.TP
.B \-\-nat\-private
The interface is the private side of a NAT router.
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " MBIT"
Report this link speed instead of the detected one.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-fdb
Do not register Train source addresses (bridge FDB entry on bridges,
additional unicast address of the interface otherwise).
.TP
.BI \-\-fdb\-hold " MS"
How long such a registration stays (default 5000 ms).
.TP
.BI \-\-observe " auto|yes|no"
auto (default): log a warning if no probe of another responder reaches a
trained test address during the first 8 rounds of a topology session (the
interface cannot observe); Train emits are still executed.
yes: no check. no: refuse Emits with Train frames.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-foreground
Do not daemonize; log to standard error unless \fB\-s\fR is given.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-syslog
Log to syslog (default when running as a daemon).
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pidfile " " \fIFILE\fR
Write the process ID to \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
More output; \-v information, \-vv debug, \-vvv decoded frames.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGHUP reloads host name and addresses, SIGTERM/SIGINT stop the daemon
(FDB entries are removed, promiscuous mode is switched off).
.SH NOTES
Needs root or CAP_NET_RAW (and CAP_NET_ADMIN for FDB entries). During a
topology test the interface is in promiscuous mode. QoS diagnostics (type
of service 2) are not implemented.
.SH SEE ALSO
[MS-LLTD] Link Layer Topology Discovery (LLTD) Protocol, Microsoft Open
Specifications.
